%S A401327 0,0,1,1,3,5,6,8,12,14,18,21
%N A401327 Folding polygons: a(n) is the maximum number of folds possible using the process described in the comments.
%C A401327 Take a regular polygon with n vertices. Select a vertex and fold it and its connecting edges across the line connecting its two neighboring vertices. The resulting polygon must be both simple and have a smaller area, otherwise the fold was illegal. Repeat until no such fold is possible. a(n) is the maximum number of folds possible.
%H A401327 Sean A. Irvine, <a href="https://github.com/archmageirvine/joeis/blob/master/src/irvine/oeis/a401/A401327.java">Java program</a> (github)
